 "scope": "Recorded proposal activation on captured live input only, not host execution or strength. 240 boards from the five live Deity 6p Continents Online Science games of 2026-11-18, every turn from the turn Writing was known to the turn the live seat placed its third Campus, each the run's events.jsonl cut right after that turn's first state row (the board the live decider saw as the turn opened) and replayed at that turn. Both arms run one frozen ci-profile civvis_orders --resumed built from the branch at b1974ea373 with the run's own requested genome (why.log line 1 forced); the on arm adds --with science-seat-campus-before-the-claims. 240 boards completed in both arms. Orders differ on 49 of them (by run: civvis-20261118T045850Z Kongo t34-75: 14 of 42; civvis-20261118T081221Z America t33-71: 10 of 39; civvis-20261118T084012Z Portugal t27-93: 6 of 67; civvis-20261118T091009Z Germany t37-79: 11 of 43; civvis-20261118T111559Z Scotland t31-79: 8 of 49). The on arms journal 47 'science-seat-campus-before-the-claims:' lines (the empire's first Campus before the floor's Settler 20, first Campus ahead of the Builder 20, first Campus ahead of the Granary 7) and the off arms 0; `produce` orders for a Campus number 16 in the off arms and 58 in the on arms (for a Library 3 and 3: the gene does not reach it). A Government Plaza is ordered into a city with one specialty slot, no Campus and no Plaza founded there yet on 5 off-arm boards (Mbamba t42, Viseu t37, Dumfries t33, Dumfries t34, Dumfries t35) and 0 on-arm boards. First three Campuses of each game (cities founded by t70): the live turn each was placed, and the first replayed board on which each arm orders it, a city never ordered in the window counted at its live turn: Kongo live t74/75/75, off arm t74/75/75, on arm t35/55/70; America live t55/68/71, off arm t49/57/68, on arm t49/49/57; Portugal live t38/86/93, off arm t38/86/93, on arm t37/38/86; Germany live t61/68/79, off arm t61/68/79, on arm t58/61/68; Scotland live t35/59/79, off arm t35/59/79, on arm t33/59/79. Boards are independent replays of the live game, so the on arm's turn is the first turn the gene would have queued the Campus, an upper bound on what a played game moves. Mean gain against the live placing 10.2 / 18.8 / 7.4 turns for the first / second / third Campus (medians 3 / 19 / 7); against the off arm's own first order 9.0 / 16.6 / 6.8 (medians 2 / 8 / 7).",
